              <item row="1" column="0">
               <widget class="QLabel" name="lblNNm">
                <property name="text">
                 <string>Value, N</string>
                </property>
               </widget>
              </item>
              <item row="1" column="1" colspan="4">
               <widget class="QLineEdit" name="Edit_ForceValue">
                <property name="toolTip">
                 <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;Specify the Force / Torque Value.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;User-defined time dependent function f(t) is supported.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Force / Torque can be defined as a combination of the math functions of time. &lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following functions can be directly entered in the input field:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;sin(t), cos(t), tan(t), sqrt(t) (Square root), exp(t) (Exponential), abs(t) (Absolute value), pi.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;It is possible to use ‘np.’ to call any standard NumPy math function, for example:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;np.cosh(t), np.round(t), np.sign(t), etc.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Following custom functions are supported in the program:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The STEP function changes smoothly between two specified values.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Syntax: step(t; t0; F0; t1; F1)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The IF function:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Syntax: if(&amp;lt;condition&amp;gt;; &amp;lt;value if less or equal to 0&amp;gt;; &amp;lt;value if greater than 0&amp;gt;).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
                </property>
                <property name="text">
                 <string>1</string>
                </property>
               </widget>
              </item>
